THIRD-PARTY CODE
----------------

This project vendors no third-party source code. It shells out to external AI
coding CLIs, which it does not distribute and which carry their own licenses
and terms of service.

Ideas and prior art that informed the design, including work this project
explicitly does not claim to have invented, are credited in
docs/PRIOR-ART.md.

The defect-coverage and single-model-recall figures cited in the README and in
any project marketing are from Tony Stone, "A Single LLM Is an Incomplete Code
Reviewer" (v2), https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21328807. They were not measured
by this project.

WHAT THIS TOOL DOES WITH YOUR CODE
----------------------------------

Cadre runs third-party AI coding tools against your source. Some of those tools
upload the code they are given to servers operated by their vendors. Cadre
itself makes no network calls — see "Nothing phones home" in the README, and
verify it rather than trusting it — but you are responsible for deciding what
you point it at.
